      Stair Baluster Spacing &amp; the 4-Inch Sphere Rule: IRC R312
    </h1>
    <p class="text-base text-gray-600 leading-relaxed max-w-3xl mb-6">
      The most frequent cause of failed building inspections on custom staircases is improper baluster spacing. Under International Residential Code (IRC) Section R312, guards are strictly mandated to prevent small children from slipping through or becoming trapped by their heads. Understanding the mathematical difference between <strong>on-center spacing vs. clear opening gap</strong> is critical to designing a safe, legal staircase.
    </p>

